    append('globe-of-invulnerability', 'CURRENT AUTHORITY: Wizard Arch Dispel Magic /cards/19 is explicitly tagged wizard-spell and has normalized spellRank3. Its3RP price and higher-target check do NOT make it a magical nonspell or rank6. Thus an outside-origin class Dispel capable of selecting this rank6 Globe is nevertheless a rank3 incoming application and is blocked at its protected anchor. From a genuinely inside authorized origin it can resolve its actual INT+PB check against DC10+target rank. Ordinary Dispel Magic is separately rank3/base5RP and can select only actual rank0-3 effects; it cannot select the rank6 Globe in the first place. An actual magical nonspell is judged by its own source; no spell rank is guessed from cost or theme. This corrects the older AC6-N02 audit wording, not the accepted class card.\n\nACCEPTED TERMINAL RETURN: ordinary Banishment BAN-CLOSE-03 has an explicit narrow exception to endpoint transport prevention at mandatory closure. This Globe does not trap an ended ordinary Banishment cell by blocking its terminal rank4 arrival. Settle all extant identities through that accepted source, including actual occupied placement/conflict handling; no physical wall, support, death or size rule is bypassed. New voluntary transport, new exile applications and other spells receive no general exception. An eventual accepted AC5 exile bridge must be refreshed before claiming its exact inherited scope.')
    replace('guards-and-wards', "This is a magical visual veil, not physical fog or an illusory depicted scene; True Seeing's ordinary illusion/darkness permissions alone do not remove it. A genuinely applicable broader sight source can work.", 'This is a NEW magical visual veil, not physical fog or an illusory depicted scene. A genuinely applicable reviewed sight source can work only within its actual scope. True Seeing remains pending in the authored index; its older proposal is comparison evidence and grants no accepted bypass here.')
    append('guards-and-wards','NEW exact visibility completion: Watch produces an ordinary visible outline of the occupied silhouette where the observer has a real sight path. This specific marker can supply that position through this parcel\'s Veil, including when the bearer separately has Invisible, but it does not make the bearer itself seen for a source requiring sight of the actual creature and does not remove Invisible\'s combat modifiers. Actual total cover hides the outline. Recognition is a fixed cast list, not shared sight or an extra targeting channel. A removed Watch application on one body cannot regenerate during its already-spent family entry interval; future genuinely new eligible entries follow the source-removal scope and live parent. Outside initiative use fixed six-second entry intervals, preserving a spent current interval when initiative begins; do not reset on recast.')
    append('forbiddance','CURRENT ALIGNMENT ORDER: evaluate the real underlying alignment history/AP-AS-01 first, then the earliest eligible active AC4 Lock/Anchor snapshot last on each locked axis under AC4-ALIGN-01. Leaving or suppressing that locking source exposes the then-live underlying value; it does not resurrect an old snapshot. A later Purge remains a real paid record beneath the lock and changes no locked effective value until the lock is inactive. For each future qualifying exposure read the actual effective complete pair at that event, never infer undefined axes.\n\nNEW ROOT CHECKPOINT: when a qualifying recipient has actually claimed the family exposure and reaches damage resolution, create one root for that recipient/event with dealer=this field\'s actual caster; snapshot that character\'s then-current unsuppressed Null Veil. Shared raw dice do not merge roots. Each later eligible pulse is a genuinely new root; the original field creation does not permanently fix every future pulse\'s Veil flag. Pure redirection/transfer descendants inherit the existing root. A suppressed event creates no damage packet and supplies no deferred pulse. This source-only periodic attached-phase checkpoint creates no companion turn, Action, Reaction or rest clock.')
    replace('resonance-seal','Propose the corresponding cross-family exclusion for the earlier unadopted Spell Seal; that earlier proposal remains preserved, and this is an explicit amendment requiring joint review.', 'The earlier Spell Seal proposal remains unadopted and unchanged. This draft proposes no automatic amendment to it: any later reciprocal exclusion requires its own explicit joint disposition. Only Resonance Seal targeting is defined here.')
    append('resonance-seal','CURRENT TRANSPORT/CLOCK LIMIT: the target is one eligible spatial magical application, not a body, vehicle, entire plane or generated Banishment cell. Sealing an eligible portal anchor cannot suppress a mandatory independent closure/expiry or preserve its destination beyond the portal source. It cannot keep ordinary Banishment open or stop BAN-CLOSE-03. A later actual suppressor must establish suppression of this Seal before the protection ceases; mere intent, caster entry into an unrelated field, or a purported high-rank dispel does not supply that premise. Suppression does not by itself prove that a dispel can operate in the same location. Pending AC5 Antimagic/Greater Dispel remains a dependency, not adopted authority for an executable removal example.')
    append('corruption-purge','CURRENT NULL BOUNDARY: Null Veil is its own accepted setting record with three exact named purge routes; it is not an ordinary Corruption application merely because it is harmful. This spell is not one of those routes and adds no fourth route. Preserve Veil, its exposure history and source protections, as well as numeric Exposure, Wounds and the intrinsic Oracle Curse. An actual source expressly creating a separate removable Corruption rider on the same character remains independently eligible: keeping Veil does not shield unrelated valid Corruption effects.')
    replace('summon-greater-air-pet','At zero HP, expiry, concentration end or actual source removal it vanishes with no corpse, item, harvest or free resummon.', 'Ordinary non-Null damage reaching zero HP ends this finite body with no corpse, item, harvest or free resummon. Qualifying Null damage instead preserves this same source/body at NullDisabled0: Incapacitated, Speed0, no Actions/Bonus Actions/Reactions/commands. Its actual Hover trait prevents a fall solely from Speed0 while the body/source remains; independent source ending still removes that support. Further qualifying Null hits cannot refresh it. Independent expiry, concentration end, replacement, dismissal or actual source removal still ends it, whether disabled or positive HP.')
    append('summon-greater-air-pet','NEW AC6-HEAL-TARGET-02: while this created finite creature body exists, expressly treat Greater Air Pet as a living ally/creature for otherwise legal ordinary HP healing, including actual Cleric Healing Rite. This is a scoped new target extension, not a claim about biology, soul, resurrection, native plane or applicability to every summon. Healing above0 ends this body\'s NullDisabled state, without resetting source deadline, HP maximum, conditions or command histories. It grants no free healing, rest pool or corpse/repair route. AC4 Water Pet/Envoy and pending AC5 Fire Pet/Champion extensions do not automatically grant this one.\n\nFor a projectile d2, actual Fate Coin can replace that one die only after its face is available to the reacting player, with a held available coin, real Reaction, perception of the actual local impact event within30feet/LoE, and the shared Mark Omen/Fate Coin original-roll-lineage guard unused. The projectile\'s earlier attack roll and the later d2 are separate roll events; multiple damage components are not multiple d2 events. A secret Director die is not revealed by the coin. A legal d2 replacement commits once and its final face owns the same event; a result1 removes the direct hit and its on-hit riders even if the original attack was natural20. A separate source-defined explosion uses its own real position/save and gets no d2 merely because a projectile delivered it.\n\nNEW suppression choice retained for joint review: full suppression of the Greater Air Pet created manifestation ends it. This differs from accepted AC4 Water Pet and the current pending AC5 Fire Pet pause model; it is deliberately source-specific and requires actual GPT agreement. Merely suppressing its projectile rider removes that defense temporarily without ending the body, while its deadline continues. The dealer of a real wind-slash root is the Pet, not its Veiled owner.')
