    append('chain-arc','NEW ROLL/ROOT COMPLETION: each successor draw is a distinct original die event, completed and any permitted replacement resolved before that successor is committed and the following candidate set is built. A legal Fate Coin replacement of a visible physical1dN changes this one index using the same original candidate ordering; never rebuild the candidate set to favor its new face. It cannot revisit the same selection after consequences or reroll a hidden die. Actual perception/30feet/LoE and the single Mark Omen/Fate Coin lineage guard remain prerequisites. A digital uniform draw is not automatically eligible for a feature expressly limited to a physical die; record the method and apply that feature\'s exact interpretation rather than grant new information or authority.\n\nAfter all legal selections and their roll replacements are final, create the instantaneous cast\'s recipient damage roots together before the first recipient damage packet: each has the caster as dealer, that caster\'s actual Veil state at this common checkpoint, its own recipient identity and the same cast lineage. Subsequent pure transfers retain those flags. Independent events later removing a selected recipient can prevent its pending packet but cannot redraw or erase the other already-established roots/arcs. No actualDamageDealt, Wound, death or resource trigger occurs merely because an identity was selected or a root allocated.')
